        },
        "pageimage": "A_Million_Open_Doors_(cover_art).jpg",
        "extract": "A Million Open Doors (1992) is a science fiction novel by American writer John Barnes, the first book of his Thousand Cultures series.  The story is told from the perspective of a maturing adult from a parochial culture who encounters many obstacles in a different and even more parochial culture which causes him to become a fully engaged citizen in the Interstellar culture. A Million Open Doors is a study of the effects of globalization.\nThe novel was nominated for the Nebula Award for Best Novel in 1992 and the Arthur C. Clarke Award in 1994.",
